    Add the folded-message claim plans for the norm parameter tables
    
    The tables plan can carry one claim per parameter: the G_u shape of the
    single-row fold (the folded row message committed with its own code, sample and
    runtime tree, folding the committed table's index), the column draw count and
    the claim kind. The claim requires the table index shape, the fit of the
    parameter width in the G_u message beside its pads, the own oracle and group
    ids and the column budget; attaching the claims changes the plan digest, and
    the claims are either both present or both absent. A unit test builds a legal
    single-row fold shape (two main message rows, one fold weight, no gamma) and
    checks the plan binding and the rejections.
    
    partial progress

